  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/... \nIssued at 1232 AM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nThe upper level low will continue to push off to the northeast \non Friday and warm air advection will start to move from west \nto east across the area. As a result highs will range from the \nmiddle 40s across central Missouri to the middle 50s across \nextreme southeastern Kansas and western Missouri Friday \nafternoon. The warming trend will continue into Saturday as \nhighs warm into the 50s with a few readings in the lower 60s.\n\nAn upper level trough will move east across the plains Saturday\nnight and across the region on Sunday. Ahead of the trough an\narea of surface low pressure will move northeast across the area\nSaturday night and off to the northeast on Sunday. Showers and\nmaybe a few rumbles of thunder will be possible across southern\nMissouri Saturday night into Sunday morning as a warmer air mass\nwill be in place. Some rain may linger across the area into\nSunday afternoon behind the departing area of surface low\npressure. Gusty northwesterly winds will also develop behind the\nlow on Sunday. The models have come into much better agreement\non the track and timing of the system with 00Z run with rain\nchances now 50 to 80% with a 10 to 20% chances for a few\nembedded thunderstorms. \n\nA warming trend will then occur early next week with highs in\nthe 50s on Monday and Tuesday as highs warm into the 60s expected\nfor the middle of next week. Highs will be coolest on Sunday\nwith reading in the upper 40s to middle 50s.",
